{
  "version": 8,
  "name": "Renters paying 30%+ of income",
  "metadata": {
    "description": "Share of renter households spending 30% or more of income on gross rent \u2014 the federal definition of rent-burdened \u2014 pale mauve to deep magenta. Measured over all 30,087 ZIP Code Tabulation Areas with a published value: 7 classes with breaks at 8.5%/34%/45%/55%/68%/88%, which fall at the 10th/29th/49th/71st/89th/95th percentile of the national distribution. 10.96% have no published value and draw in neutral gray rather than as a low value. 39.44% of ZIP Code Tabulation Areas have a coefficient of variation above 0.3 at this geography, too many to fade without washing the map out, so read pct_rent_burdened_moe in the GeoParquet before drawing a conclusion from any single ZCTA.",
    "portolan:column": "pct_rent_burdened",
    "portolan:breaks": [
      8.5,
      34,
      45,
      55,
      68,
      88
    ]
  },
